extraction_notes: "WB9 South America 2 printed 128-129 (cache p128-p129, page_offset 0); the lore opens on 128, the whole stat block is on 129, the Plains ''Borg heading following it. Printed 129 checked against a 110 dpi render; the OCR agreed on every number. No gaucho class was in production on 2026-09-25. || XP: the Gaucho ladder on printed 192, read off a render, as briefed. || GROUP: the book files the O.C.C. under ''Common O.C.C.s in Santiago and Cordoba'', not under a group heading; stored as men-of-arms (a horseman and knife fighter who works as ranch guard, scout and mercenary). No sdc_base or mdc_base is printed, so men_of_arms: true (the core 3D6), with the printed 4D6 S.D.C. as a pool bonus on top. || BONUSES: +2 P.S., +1 P.E., +4D6 S.D.C., +2 initiative, +2 roll with impact, +2 pull punch, +3 save vs horror factor stored unconditionally. The +1 strike/parry from horseback (hand to hand only) and the knife bonuses (+1 strike/parry, +2 strike thrown, paired knives) are conditional and are abilities. || SKILLS: Spanish (98%) as Language: Spanish 98, the row this book''s other classes use. Literacy: Spanish (+15%) as Literacy: Native Language 40+15, the precedent for a printed native-language literacy. Basic Math 45+10; Horsemanship (+25%) as Horsemanship: General 40+25; one Pilot of choice +10; Tracking (+15%) as Tracking (people) 25+15, the catalog''s only tracking row; Detect Ambush 30+10; Wilderness Survival 30+15. W.P. Bola exists; the ''treat as Archery & Targeting'' remark is its note. Hand to Hand: Expert converts to Martial Arts or Assassin (if evil) for one other skill. || RELATED: seven, plus one W.P. and one skill at level 3, two at 6, one at 9 and 12 (stored as 2/2/1/1; that one of the level-3 picks is a W.P. is the note - a schedule entry carries no category). Bonuses as printed: Communications +10, Domestic +10, Pilot +10, Pilot Related +10, Technical +5, Wilderness +10; Rogue, Science and W.P. any; Electrical Basic Electronics only; Espionage Detect Concealment and Sniper only; Mechanical Automotive only (Automotive Mechanics); Medical First Aid and Paramedic only; Physical any except Acrobatics; Military none. The list names no Horsemanship or Cowboy line, so neither category is granted. || SECONDARY: two each at levels 1, 3, 6 and 10 (count 2, schedule 3/6/10), limited as the related list, no bonuses. || EQUIPMENT: medium body armor as a choice led by gaucho-combat-armor (this book, printed 166); two vibro-knives; two regular knives; an energy weapon of choice from a catalog set; four E-clips; a non-energy weapon of choice from a catalog set; a mount or vehicle from the catalog set (no cyber-horse or robot horse row). The camp kit is stored item by item: shovel, hatchet for the wood axe, lighter and matches, flashlight, sleeping bag, survival knife, rations (2D6 days, in the note), canteen; two sets of work/travel clothes and one of good clothes. The two ENERGY BOLAS have no catalog row (the book gives them no stats here) and are not stubbed; the plain Bola row is not a substitute. || MONEY: 2D4x1000 credits. class-check warns that a race stating its own starting_money would win a pairing; the book does not make the gaucho replace its race, so that is correct and no supersedes_race is set. || CYBERNETICS: 1D4 cybernetic implants and two bionic items short of partial or full reconstruction; the app has no implant catalog pick, so this is an ability and the limit a restriction."
---

## Lore

The gaucho is the plainsman of South America, a horseman of the cattle
ranches known for his skill with the knife and the bola. Before the Great
Cataclysm the breed had faded into folklore and tourist shows; the chaos that
followed the Coming of the Rifts brought it back. Ranchers now face bandits,
rustlers, alien raiders, predators and things from beyond the Rifts, and the
men who guard their herds have traded plain steel for vibro-blades and energy
snares.

Many still ride real horses, but motorcycles, off-road vehicles, robot horses
and armored cyber-horses are common, and the wealthy landowners who employ
gauchos are glad to equip them with energy weapons, implants and bionics. Most
work the ranches that feed the Silver River Republics; others drift into work
as bodyguards, bounty hunters, scouts and mercenaries, where their riding,
tracking and fighting skills are always in demand.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'gaucho');


